%I A399429 #22 Sep 10 2026 18:48:35
%S A399429 1,2,3,6,12,16,18,21,25,28,31,35,38,41,43,45,47,50,53,55,57,62,65,70,
%T A399429 72,75,77,79,82,84,86,89,92,94,96,100,102,104,106,108,113,117,119,121,
%U A399429 124,127,129,132,134,138,141,144,146,149,152,155,159,162,164,167
%N A399429 Indices of record low-water marks of the sequence abs((sin(p))^p) where p is the numerator of the k-th convergent to Pi/2, starting from k = 1.
%C A399429 After the two initial terms 1 and 2, this sequence is exactly the list of k for which the denominator A096463(k-1) is even.
%H A399429 Jwalin Bhatt, <a href="/A399429/b399429.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..636</a>
%e A399429 The first few values of abs((sin(p))^p), where p is the numerator of the k-th convergent to Pi/2 and D is its denominator:
%e A399429   | k  | p       | D       | abs((sin(p))^p)     |
%e A399429   |----|---------|---------|---------------------|
%e A399429   | 1  | 1       | 1       | 0.841470985         |
%e A399429   | 2  | 2       | 1       | 0.826821810         |
%e A399429   | 3  | 3       | 2       | 0.00281038473       |
%e A399429   | 4  | 11      | 7       | 0.999892277         |
%e A399429   | 5  | 344     | 219     | 0.996682290         |
%e A399429   | 6  | 355     | 226     | 1.3126*10^-1605     |
%e A399429 and the record low points are at k = 1, 2, 3, 6, ...
%t A399429 Join[{1, 2}, Flatten @ Position[Denominator @ Convergents[Pi/2, 170], _?EvenQ]]
%o A399429 (Python)
%o A399429 from sympy import pi, continued_fraction_iterator, continued_fraction_convergents
%o A399429 from itertools import islice
%o A399429 cf_iter = continued_fraction_convergents(continued_fraction_iterator(pi/2))
%o A399429 A399429 = [1, 2] + [k for k, f in enumerate(islice(cf_iter, 60), start=1) if f.denominator % 2 == 0]
%o A399429 print(A399429)
%Y A399429 Cf. A096456, A096463, A399391.
%K A399429 nonn,new
%O A399429 1,2
%A A399429 _Jwalin Bhatt_, Aug 28 2026
